WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.435
-Our first guest, tonight,
is an Emmy-winning

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.571
and Tony-nominated
comedian and writer

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:06.773
who you know from her work
on "Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:09.743
"30 Rock," "Girls5eva,"
and "Mean Girls,"

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:11.678
both the movie
and the Broadway musical.

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.646
She's the co-creator
of "Mr. Mayor,"

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:16.449
which airs Tuesday nights
at 8:30 p.m., here on NBC.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.650
Please welcome back to the show,

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.986
our very good friend,
Tina Fey, everybody.

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:21.821
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:31.831 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:39.204 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:39.204 --> 00:00:41.640
-Hi!
-It is so good to see you!

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.242
-It's so nice to see you.

00:00:43.242 --> 00:00:44.610
-I've seen you in person
a few times.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:45.778
-Yeah.
-The last time you were on

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:48.347
the show was via Zoom.
-Yes.

00:00:48.347 --> 00:00:50.483
-And your daughter Penelope
did that lovely thing

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.218
that was happening in
the early days of the pandemic.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.853
She just fully crashed
the interview.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.488
-She just fully entered
the Zoom, yeah.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:58.124
-Yeah. And was not very
complimentary to either of us.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.491
-No, she entered the Zoom.

00:00:59.491 --> 00:01:01.761
I believe she was wearing, like,
a Colonial-lady outfit.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.062
-Yeah.
-Because -- as one does.

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:05.265
And then she just got behind me
and just went --

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:07.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.536
And did, like, a slow...
-Yeah.

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:10.836
-...slow exit.
You know.

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:12.572
-Does she like her time
on camera?

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.040
She did seem very comfortable.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.243
-She was a little too
comfortable at that time, yeah.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.444
Yeah, they both are.

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:20.746
You know, Penelope ended up
on "Girls5eva."

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:25.217
But, yeah, Alice and Penelope
are both really funny.

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:26.585
They have a great
sense of humor.

00:01:26.585 --> 00:01:28.988
I am embargoed from speaking
about them on talk shows.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.323
-Gotcha.
-Because that's what happens.

00:01:31.323 --> 00:01:33.359
Like, they're such a gold mine
for stories, at first.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.827
-Yes.
-And then someday,

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:38.264
Axel's gonna come to you and be
like, "I'm the Lobby Baby?"

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.966
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.667
-"Really, Dad?"
-It's gonna be a problem.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.137
-"I'm the Lobby Baby?"
And you're like, "Uh, well..."

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:45.972
and you have to backpedal.
[ Laughs ]

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:48.141
-I'm just hoping Netflix won't
be around by then, you know?

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:49.208
-Well --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.276
-Hey, can we talk about this?

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.277
Are you allowed
to talk about that?

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.611
Yeah, okay. So, that is --
-Okay.

00:01:52.611 --> 00:01:53.846
-Again, back in the days
when I used to talk about them,

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:55.381
this is the other thing that,
like, such a --

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.450
such a weird New York childhood
that our kids have that like...

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.685
-Yes.
-my older daughter is 16 now,

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:03.356
and she was talking
to another teenager,

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.258
and he was saying like, "Yeah,
it was hard 'cause, you know,

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.392
like, I got made into a meme."

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.693
She's like, "Yeah,
I was a meme once, too."

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:09.695
Like, kids are growing up, like,
being like,

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:11.998
"Yeah, I was memed once."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:14.100
And I was like, "Oh, yeah."
And I don't --

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.969
And I knew she had been a meme
when she was little.

00:02:16.969 --> 00:02:19.172
And I don't know when she
found out she was a meme.

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.740
-Right,
'cause you didn't tell her.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.575
-No!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:25.244
Because it wasn't my fault.
But she was a fantastic meme.

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:26.578
-It's a really good meme.
Anybody --

00:02:26.578 --> 00:02:28.747
Does anyone remember this meme?
What's your camera?

00:02:28.747 --> 00:02:29.882
-Here, right over there.
Go over there.

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:32.752
-I don't work here.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.620
I mean, that's a fantastic meme.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.156
Even this, I might still get in
trouble for reshowing this.

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:38.424
-Yeah.
-Oh, that camera, sure.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.526
-But she looks really good.
Now is that --

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:41.994
Can we assume -- is that you?

00:02:41.994 --> 00:02:43.796
-That's me looking
just bedraggled.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.264
-Yeah.
-And I think part of --

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:47.566
part of the meme was, like,
she was living high on the hog,

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:49.235
and I was bedraggled.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.938
Thank you for
cropping me out of that.

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:53.339
-I do love it.
I mean, it is --

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.774
Somebody really nailed it
when they were like,

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.075
"This girl's gonna be a meme."
-And there were ones, like,

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:58.344
they put that next to, like,
Michael Cera or, like,

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.546
next to, like,
Happy Leo DiCaprio.

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:02.415
It's a whole thing.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:04.851
-Now, you did a thing
that I think is very kind

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:05.985
of a parent to do.

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.253
You allowed your children
to get a pet.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:08.387
What kind of pet do you have?

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:11.190
-Oh, yeah, I own
a bearded dragon now, Seth.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.725
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:16.429
-Who wanted the bearded dragon?
-Penelope was very...

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.863
-Okay.
-...is into -- very much into

00:03:17.863 --> 00:03:19.231
the lizard, reptile lifestyle.

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:20.833
-And she was specific
of this one?

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:24.237
-Yes. Um, [bleep] YouTube
will tell you a lot about

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:25.971
different kinds of
lizards and stuff.

00:03:25.971 --> 00:03:27.807
And --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.842
-What kind -- is it
a boy lizard, a girl lizard?

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:33.346
-It's -- their name is Herman.
-Okay.

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:35.381
-And they come --
they're like this big.

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.616
-Okay.
-And then it's, like, you know,

00:03:37.616 --> 00:03:39.518
those little sponge capsules
that you put in water,

00:03:39.518 --> 00:03:41.854
and then it's like -- bwaaarrr!

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:45.357
He's already this big.
I think, from what I'm told,

00:03:45.357 --> 00:03:47.659
bearded dragons, they don't
have a gender at first.

00:03:47.659 --> 00:03:48.861
-Okay.
-Their genitals develop

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.229
over time.
-Gotcha.

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:52.398
-We decided that their name
is Herman, no matter what.

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:55.634
-Okay.
-None of us is really into,

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:57.470
like, digging for the genitals.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.504
-Right?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.239
-We're just kind of like,
"Whatever."

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:01.307
It doesn't matter.
-Right.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:03.042
-They live alone.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:04.410
In a tank.
-Yeah.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:08.014
-So -- And --
-Yeah, Herman's not filling out

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:09.314
a Tinder profile or anything.

00:04:09.314 --> 00:04:11.317
-Exactly, Herman's not looking
to meet people.

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.552
-[ Laughs ]
-By the way, my mom

00:04:13.552 --> 00:04:15.054
is staying with me right now.
And guess what --

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:17.690
she's gonna say,
"Why did I see your elbows?"

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.593
And I'm gonna say,
"I don't know."

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:21.827
-Yeah.
-Did you like them, though?

00:04:21.827 --> 00:04:23.295
-It's great.
By the way, you came out,

00:04:23.295 --> 00:04:24.764
and I saw it,
and I thought to myself,

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:27.100
"That is a wonderful
sartorial choice."

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.267
-Yeah, thanks.
-'Cause that's fashion

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:29.568
right there.
-Fashion.

00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:31.137
-Fashion.
-Yes.

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:32.805
-But that is a very big asterisk

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:33.906
that your mother
is staying with you.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.274
-Oh, this is not for anyone's --

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.577
Anyone's mom
is gonna be like, "What?"

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:38.745
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:40.980
-That is her "Euphoria,"
that you're wearing that.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.314
-This is her "Euphoria."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.314 --> 00:04:43.650
"I'm not gonna understand it!

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.351
I'm not gonna
try to understand it!

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:47.553
I won't even look at it."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:49.588
Um, lizards, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:49.588 --> 00:04:52.491
So you -- I'm gonna move --
Can I move off from lizards?

00:04:52.491 --> 00:04:54.193
Do you have more to add?
-Please.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.429
No, I will say that the only
thing about lizards is that you

00:04:56.429 --> 00:05:00.266
also then get to be the owner
of 60 or 70

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:02.268
live crickets every week also.
-Oh.

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:03.803
Now, I'm assuming
these are not around

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:05.671
for the lizard's companionship.
-They are --

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:07.707
No, they're their food, yeah.

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:09.509
-So you get 60 crickets a week.
-Yeah.

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:10.777
-Do the crickets --
-You have to go get them.

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:12.644
-Okay.
-And then they sing all night

00:05:12.644 --> 00:05:14.746
in your apartment.
And it's so sad,

00:05:14.746 --> 00:05:16.315
because they don't know
they're on death row.

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:18.050
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:19.719
They're singing like
they're in Central Park.

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:21.553
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.553 --> 00:05:23.289
Death row.
-That is heartbreaking.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.624
-It's heartbreaking.
-'Cause you know.

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:27.593
-I know what's going down.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.127
-I don't know what kind of
genitals Herman has,

00:05:29.127 --> 00:05:31.063
but I know what's gonna go down
with those crickets.

00:05:31.063 --> 00:05:32.431
-You know he's got a mouth.
-Yeah.

00:05:32.431 --> 00:05:34.166
-They have a mouth.

00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:35.200
-I should have brought
a picture,

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.136
'cause when Herman eats,

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:38.938
they look exactly
like Don Rickles.

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:40.406
-Really?
-Yeah. I'll send you a picture.

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:41.740
-Okay, great.
-Yeah.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:44.176
-I have a lot of questions
about "Girls5eva."

00:05:44.176 --> 00:05:45.477
We'll be right back
with more from Tina Fey.

00:05:45.477 --> 00:05:47.580
-Probably more about lizards.
-And more about lizards.

